Target-option check of each candidate Run with the options in ABCD and DCBA order, keeping their
labels unchanged. For Nonliteral distractors, “bystander”
is replaced with “nonliteral” throughout the prompt. Prompt. You are labeling which answer-choice concept is evoked by an unrelated bystander sentence in a medical multiple-choice question. Medical question: {question} Answer choices (the display order may be shuffled; preserve the printed labels): {choices} Bystander sentence: {sentence} Independently determine which answer-choice concept the bystander sentence most strongly evokes. Do not solve the medical question. If exactly one option is evoked, use its printed label. Use NONE if no option is meaningfully evoked and MULTI if multiple options are comparably evoked. Return only a JSON object with exactly these fields: {"primary_evoked_option":"A|B|C|D|NONE|MULTI","evoked_options":["A|B|C|D"],"relation_type":"LEXICAL_DIRECT|MORPHOLOGICAL|SEMANTIC|NONE|MULTI","strength":"strong|weak|none"}
